      "tier": 2,
      "title": "Why Stripe Cut 500,000 Internal Docs Down to 5,000?",
      "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=btsbU79zuWg",
      "published_at": "2026-11-13T00:15:21+00:00",
      "author": "AAIF Live",
      "summary": "What happens when AI agents start relying on the same messy docs your team already struggles to search?\n\nDemetrios hops into a Waymo in San Francisco with Dave Nunez, founder and CEO of Falconer and co-author of Documentation for Developers. They talk about why developers and agents need different things from docs, why agents sometimes skip up-to-date instructions, and how a stale internal document can contribute to a production incident.\n\nDave shares how Stripe cut roughly 500,000 internal docs down to 5,000 worth maintaining. The conversation also covers how to capture the reasoning behind engineering decisions, when a diagram beats a wall of text, and who owns the fallout when an agent acts on bad information.\n\nTimestamps:\n[00:00] Hopping into a Waymo in San Francisco\n[00:24] Meet Dave, founder of Falconer\n[01:15] Why internal docs matter for AI agents\n[03:24] What humans and agents each need from docs\n[05:46] Testing how well agents use developer tools\n[07:01] Why agents skip the latest docs\n[09:42] Decision records and the reasoning behind the code\n[14:04] Cleaning up stale docs and broken search\n[15:29] How Stripe went from 500,000 docs to 5,000\n[17:02] When a diagram beats a 10-page doc\n[18:53] How conflicting docs can lead to an incident\n[20:42] Who owns reliability when an agent makes a mistake?\n[24:01] Treating documentation as part of the product\n[26:38] Giving readers an escape hatch\n[27:27] The cost of AI-generated fluff\n[29:36] Wrap-up and post-show chat",
